    <author><name>AATF AI News Aggregator</name></author>
    <summary type="html"><![CDATA[<p><strong>Launch of the week — Bot Screen / desktop passthrough in Hermes Desktop:</strong> The official <strong>NousResearch</strong> <a href="https://hermes-agent-news.vercel.app/?date=2026-09-24&amp;category=social#item-ef6b4179c4fa" class="internal-link" rel="noopener noreferrer">announcement of <strong>Bot Screen</strong></a> (real-time streaming of any agent's browser or terminal session) was the top post of the batch, with <strong>Teknium</strong>'s companion <a href="https://hermes-agent-news.vercel.app/?date=2026-09-24&amp;category=social#item-4784626f2a61" class="internal-link" rel="noopener noreferrer">reveal of the interactive desktop passthrough</a> — visually and interactively accessing the same machine your <strong>Hermes Agent</strong> works on — pulling 1,148+ likes. <strong>@tonbistudio</strong>'s <a href="https://hermes-agent-news.vercel.app/?date=2026-09-24&amp;category=social#item-d84a2bc0a85d" class="internal-link" rel="noopener noreferrer">walkthrough video and docs</a> were amplified by both <strong>NousResearch</strong> (544 likes, ~46k views) and <a href="https://hermes-agent-news.vercel.app/?date=2026-09-24&amp;category=social#item-d03d44ef66a9" class="internal-link" rel="noopener noreferrer"><strong>Teknium</strong></a>, making this feature the undisputed center of attention.</p>
<p><strong>Community OSS — oh-my-hermes &amp; Jev ecosystem:</strong> <strong>rlaope</strong> <a href="https://hermes-agent-news.vercel.app/?date=2026-09-24&amp;category=social#item-99948938337f" class="internal-link" rel="noopener noreferrer">open-sourced <strong>jeval</strong></a> (Jev evaluation/visualization) and shipped <a href="https://hermes-agent-news.vercel.app/?date=2026-09-24&amp;category=social#item-415aecf318f8" class="internal-link" rel="noopener noreferrer"><strong>oh-my-hermes</strong> support for <strong>Jev-Skills</strong> and <strong>model routing</strong></a> (Jev models/aliases, skills/plugins, workflows), positioning OMH as the <a href="https://hermes-agent-news.vercel.app/?date=2026-09-24&amp;category=social#item-b4d141253a4f" class="internal-link" rel="noopener noreferrer">all-in-one plugin for hermes-agent power users</a> — the strongest original-contribution thread of the period.</p>
<p><strong>Maintainer engagement &amp; official support:</strong> <strong>Teknium</strong> directly <a href="https://hermes-agent-news.vercel.app/?date=2026-09-24&amp;category=social#item-d5a2f794eeec" class="internal-link" rel="noopener noreferrer">rebutted a reported cache problem</a> (demanding reproducible issue-tracker paths, signaling thorough testing) and confirmed a rapid fix, while <strong>NousResearch</strong> <a href="https://hermes-agent-news.vercel.app/?date=2026-09-24&amp;category=social#item-768697783517" class="internal-link" rel="noopener noreferrer">dispensed a practical usage tip</a> (<strong>Hermes</strong> via <strong>iMessage</strong> with any model, 121 likes) and <strong>Teknium</strong> <a href="https://hermes-agent-news.vercel.app/?date=2026-09-24&amp;category=social#item-992950038a21" class="internal-link" rel="noopener noreferrer">corrected a public misattribution</a>, clarifying the work in question is built by <strong>Nous Research</strong>, not Anthropic.</p>
<p><strong>Sentiment:</strong> Overwhelmingly positive and long-awaited — <strong>Teknium</strong>'s <a href="https://hermes-agent-news.vercel.app/?date=2026-09-24&amp;category=social#item-48968e1c836e" class="internal-link" rel="noopener noreferrer">"Much needed!"</a> (202 likes, ~20k views) and <a href="https://hermes-agent-news.vercel.app/?date=2026-09-24&amp;category=social#item-015fe011793b" class="internal-link" rel="noopener noreferrer">"Impressive!"</a> endorsement captured launch enthusiasm. Remaining posts (<a href="https://hermes-agent-news.vercel.app/?date=2026-09-24&amp;category=social#item-486ebb464590" class="internal-link" rel="noopener noreferrer">emoji-only replies</a>, <a href="https://hermes-agent-news.vercel.app/?date=2026-09-24&amp;category=social#item-119341252aeb" class="internal-link" rel="noopener noreferrer">bare link reposts</a>, <a href="https://hermes-agent-news.vercel.app/?date=2026-09-24&amp;category=social#item-921e5927b0af" class="internal-link" rel="noopener noreferrer">engagement-bait prompts</a>, vague <a href="https://hermes-agent-news.vercel.app/?date=2026-09-24&amp;category=social#item-797e0ee6c95e" class="internal-link" rel="noopener noreferrer">Opus 5.5/Claude Code takes</a>) carried little informational value and were excluded from the ranking.</p>]]></summary>
